                <pb facs="1236" n="1220" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg1220"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">460.509/11–2851: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bonsal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-11-28T20:00:00+01:00">November 28,
                            1951—8 p. m</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3189. No distribution outside Dept. For Camp and Vernon. Excon. USDel
                    informed today that Harriman has (1) agreed make primary lists available all
                    countries, in view Dept concurrence; (2) agreed leave question of classification
                    open until he returns in second week Dec; and (3) signed title II “short list”
                    as originally prepared, with addition item 2073, owing to strong views expressed
                    by other agencies and Cong Battle. USDel
                    understands Harriman not convinced on merits “short list” as against long and
                    desires discuss matter further when returns.</p>
                <p>Longer list II which USDel was asked prepare
                    has been given Tannenwald, who is leaving tomorrow.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept 3189, rptd info Rome 257 for Linder.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bonsal</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
